From 3a08c1480d554a0e712e0f44e5d6330f46b142ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 00:52:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Lakka: Switch: reboot2payload integration

Adds a small misc/reboot2payload module that drives the Tegra pmc_r2p
sysfs interface so RetroArch can reboot directly into a chosen Hekate
payload (a hekate_ipl.ini launch entry, a bootloader/ini/<name>.ini
config, or the Hekate menu itself), and threads it through the menu:

  * New CMD_EVENT_REBOOT2PAYLOAD command. The Reboot menu entry now
    routes through this handler on Lakka Switch; vanilla Lakka still
    uses CMD_EVENT_REBOOT.

  * Switch Options gets a new 'Reboot Payload' entry. Left/Right
    cycle through parsed entries and mirror the selection into
    settings (uints.reboot_payload_kind +
    arrays.reboot_payload_name) so it survives across launches.

  * A new 'Force Reboot to Lakka if Update Exists' toggle. When on
    (the default) and an update tarball is staged in
    /storage/.update, the payload selection is overridden so the
    initramfs picks up the update on the way back into Lakka.

  * menu_action_setting_disp_reboot in menu_cbs_get_value.c is
    extended to render the selected payload name in the value
    column of the main Reboot entry on Switch (or 'Install Update'
    when the update toggle would override the selection).

  * On startup, retroarch.c parses /flash/bootloader/* and restores
    the persisted selection by name (falling back to the cmdline
    self entry when the saved name is gone).

Rebased on top of the sys-clk merge:

  * Module include lines that used to sit alongside cpufreq.h /
    gpufreq.h now sit in dedicated HAVE_LAKKA_SWITCH blocks next
    to the unified sys-clk.h include.

  * The Makefile.common HAVE_LAKKA_SWITCH section was deleted by
    sys-clk; it is re-created here just for the reboot2payload
    object.

  * BIND_ACTION cases for MENU_ENUM_LABEL_REBOOT_PAYLOAD live in
    their own HAVE_LAKKA_SWITCH blocks rather than being folded
    into the GPU HAVE_LAKKA_SWITCH block that no longer exists.

  * The retroarch.c init site for r2p_refresh_payloads /
    r2p_restore_persisted_selection sits in a new HAVE_LAKKA_SWITCH
    block after the unified sys-clk init, instead of inside the
    deleted gpu_scaling_driver_init block.

No behaviour changes outside Lakka Switch builds.
